# Crontab example for running daily reminders
# Copy and customize this file based on your needs

# Format: minute hour day_of_month month day_of_week command

# ========== OPTION 1: Run at 8:00 AM daily ==========
0 8 * * * cd /Users/phihongthai/Documents/claude/telegrambotEffort && /usr/bin/python3 remind.py >> remind.log 2>&1

# ========== OPTION 2: Run at 8:00 PM daily ==========
# 0 20 * * * cd /Users/phihongthai/Documents/claude/telegrambotEffort && /usr/bin/python3 remind.py >> remind.log 2>&1

# ========== OPTION 3: Run at 7:00 PM daily ==========
# 0 19 * * * cd /Users/phihongthai/Documents/claude/telegrambotEffort && /usr/bin/python3 remind.py >> remind.log 2>&1

# ========== OPTION 4: Run multiple times a day ==========
# Morning (8 AM) and Evening (8 PM)
# 0 8,20 * * * cd /Users/phihongthai/Documents/claude/telegrambotEffort && /usr/bin/python3 remind.py >> remind.log 2>&1

# ========== OPTION 5: Run every 6 hours ==========
# 0 */6 * * * cd /Users/phihongthai/Documents/claude/telegrambotEffort && /usr/bin/python3 remind.py >> remind.log 2>&1

# INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Edit this file with your desired schedule
# 2. Copy and paste into: crontab -e
# 3. Make sure to export TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN before running
#
# Example setup:
# - Open terminal
# - Run: export TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="your_bot_token"
# - Run: crontab -e
# - Paste your chosen cron line
# - Save and exit
#
# To verify cron is running:
# - Check logs: tail -f remind.log
# - List active crons: crontab -l
